Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] Real sandhi at the Parigraha iti-junction; auto-detect
 sutra 10.8 bahumadhyagata

Read Uvata's own bhashya on sutras 10.8-10.11 and 11.23/11.37-43 directly
(previously only the bare sutra text was on file for most of these).
Two source-verified fixes:

- get_sthitopasthita()/get_upasthita() were rendering "word iti word" as
  a fixed unsandhied template. That happened to match Uvata's only two
  examples this engine had been checked against (vibhaavaso, baahuu) --
  both independently pragrhya, which is exactly why they resist sandhi.
  His non-pragrhya examples on 10.8/10.16 ("ca iti ca" -> "ceti ca",
  "cit iti cit" -> "cidati cit", "vaa iti vaa" -> "veti vaa", "purojitii
  iti" -> "purojitiiti") show real sandhi applies at this junction unless
  the word is pragrhya. Fixed to call the real samhita_join engine
  (apply_sandhi=False bypass for a caller-confirmed pragrhya word);
  verified it reproduces all four citations exactly with no new special
  casing. Re-ran regenerate_krama_rv_1_1.py: no new phonology
  regressions, only the two already-documented pair-level differences
  from the architecture doc's sec.6.6 remain.

- Implemented sutra 10.8's bahumadhyagata auto-detection for real
  (detect_bahumadhyagata(), a small closed particle class -- ca/vaa/cit
  -- sourced directly from Uvata's three worked examples), replacing
  Test G's old guessed expectation (which matched no actual citation).
  generate_ardharca() now calls it automatically when
  bahumadhyagata_positions isn't supplied. Test G now legitimately
  passes.

Updated the stale "at least 7 of 9 verses exact-match the old
hand-aligned file" regression test, which can never pass again now that
the correct rendering differs from that file's wrong iti-spacing
convention at every Parigraha unit, with a check that every remaining
pair-level diff is one of the two already-known cases -- still fails
loudly on a genuinely new regression.

Two harder items surfaced with strong new sourcing (11.23's natva-
restoration-on-retake, 11.43's shuddhakshara-augment insertion) plus a
real open question about whether 10.10-11 narrows the existing 10.3
aa-exception mechanism -- not implemented without either a general
Paninian rule or a closed citation, sent out as a scoped, fully
self-contained code-only prompt (GEMINI_CHATGPT_TASK_PROMPT_V3.md) per
standing instruction to route stuck items externally rather than guess.

Full detail in dge/RV_PRATISHAKHYA_KRAMA_ARCHITECTURE.md sec.6.12.

